== 2. The three points I agreed with in #726, against the diff (Source) ==
1. A late retry yields: on a run after a cut, take checks under both locks that the spare
   is still the spare at the generation the entry names, that the seat is held by the old
   session at its generation or by no one, with no binding at a later one, and that no
   later takeover of the seat is in the record. Otherwise the takeover is superseded:
   nothing written, nothing moved, the reason said, and back lists it so.
2. Decided from the record: after any error, take looks in the verified record for its own
   entry. The table's rows are "before the entry" and "after the entry, whatever the append
   returned". A torn record refuses take until repaired.
3. away stays terminal-only: "or no terminal to ask at" is gone.
Also in: my note from #719, that the spare's binding is written last so its listener can
still wake it; and the lock order under the fences.

